{"id":7,"date":"2017-02-27T07:32:34","date_gmt":"2017-02-27T07:32:34","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/francine-feminine.com\/?page_id=7"},"modified":"2017-05-08T17:38:54","modified_gmt":"2017-05-08T09:38:54","slug":"indications","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/francine-feminine.com\/indications\/","title":{"rendered":"Indications"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><div  class=\"fusion-fullwidth fullwidth-box nonhundred-percent-fullwidth\"  style='background-color: #e8478a;background-position: center center;background-repeat: no-repeat;padding-top:40px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:20px;padding-left:0px;margin-bottom: 0px;margin-top: 0px;'><div class=\"fusion-builder-row fusion-row \"><div  class=\"fusion-layout-column fusion_builder_column fusion_builder_column_1_1  fusion-one-full fusion-column-first fusion-column-last 1_1\"  style='margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;'>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"fusion-column-wrapper\"  style=\"padding: 0 3% 0 3%;background-position:left top;background-repeat:no-repeat;-webkit-background-size:cover;-moz-background-size:cover;-o-background-size:cover;background-size:cover;\"  data-bg-url=\"\">\n\t\t\t\t<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ffffff;\"><em><strong>Francine Gentle Cleansing Care<\/strong><\/em> is designed to intimate confidence and best hygiene for daily care including in multiple situations that develop during feminine life including pregnancy, menopause but also during sports (perspiring, swimming pool, chemicals).<\/span><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ffffff;\"><br \/>\nTo keep away the common discomfort in your intimate areas (itching, irritation, abnormal odor etc), it is important to adopt the appropriate hygiene practices and use the most appropriate gentle cleansing care.<br \/>\n<\/span><\/p>\n<div class=\"fusion-clearfix\"><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div><\/div><\/div><div  class=\"fusion-fullwidth fullwidth-box nonhundred-percent-fullwidth fusion-equal-height-columns\"  style='background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0);background-position: center center;background-repeat: no-repeat;padding-top:20px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:20px;padding-left:0px;'><div class=\"fusion-builder-row fusion-row \"><div  class=\"fusion-layout-column fusion_builder_column fusion_builder_column_1_2  fusion-one-half fusion-column-first 1_2\"  style='margin-top:40px;margin-bottom:40px;width:50%;width:calc(50% - ( ( 4% ) * 0.5 ) );margin-right: 4%;'>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"fusion-column-wrapper\"  style=\"background-position:left top;background-repeat:no-repeat;-webkit-background-size:cover;-moz-background-size:cover;-o-background-size:cover;background-size:cover;\"  data-bg-url=\"\">\n\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"color: #e8478a;\"><strong>Discomfort can have many causes like:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using harsh soap (such as regular bath soap) to wash intimate areas<\/li>\n<li>An imbalance in the vaginal flora<\/li>\n<li>Prolonged contact with feminine discharge<\/li>\n<li>Using perfumed sanitary pad<\/li>\n<li>Wearing synthetic underwear or tight jeans<\/li>\n<li>Using a fabric softener or detergent containing high levels of fragrance<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"color: #e8478a;\"><strong>Simple steps that can prevent discomfort:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Only wash external areas (the vulva and the area around the anus).<\/li>\n<li>Wash intimate areas a maximum of twice daily, morning and evening. Washing more frequently can cause irritations.<\/li>\n<li>Use soap-free cleansing products that are formulated for intimate areas and that contain moisturizing and soothing active ingredient.<\/li>\n<li>If you are prescribed antibiotics, inform your doctor that you are prone to irritations in intimate areas.<\/li>\n<li>Avoid douching, which can upset the balance of vaginal flora.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<div class=\"fusion-clearfix\"><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div><div  class=\"fusion-layout-column fusion_builder_column fusion_builder_co